    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The trip is a genuine route deviation and the rider is refunded SGD 9.10.\n\nThe evidence. The GPS trace for TRP-02804 (EV-GPS-02804) runs from the recorded pickup at 16:04:05 to the recorded drop-off at 16:42:05 on 27 August 2026 and measures 29.13 km. The booked optimal route on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02804) is 22.1 km. Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs over the rounded 29.1 km copy on the trip record, so the excess is 7.03 km, or 31.81% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (over 0.8 km and over 20%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not material: 31.81% is below the 50% gate and 7.03 km is below the 8.0 km gate. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) - 229 fixes at 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s - so no independent corroboration is required.\n\nNo excuse applies. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02804) holds no messages, so POL-RD-04 cannot run. The trip record shows no amended pickup or drop-off and no amended optimal distance, so POL-RD-05 does not apply; the vehicle is RYDE_X with no pooled itinerary, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The driver's account (heavy traffic, another road) is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else. No advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-02804-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run, and an assertion citing no advisory and no evidence ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The traffic assertion is discarded, no advisory was on file, and the excess is not reduced.\n\nThe refund. The fare is METERED (EV-FARE-02804), so POL-RD-02 governs and the refund is arithmetic. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 22.1 + 0.28 x 29.8) x 1.2 surge, read from the fare breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.50 ERP on the optimal route = 36.7628. Charged total = 45.82. Refund = 45.82 - 36.7628 = 9.0572, rounded up to SGD 9.10. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below 90% of charged_total, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 9.10. The one ERP line (PIE Eunos westbound, SGD 1.50) is on the optimal route - the nearest trace fix is 35.32 m away, inside the 250 m radius - and is already inside the recomputed fare; under POL-RD-09(1) it is itemised for transparency and never added on top.\n\nPoints argued. The rider's submission that the refund is capped at the SGD 8.50 contested is rejected: no clause makes the amount in dispute a ceiling, and POL-RD-02 fixes the refund arithmetically at the SGD 9.10 the money block records as payable. The submission that the trip record and the fare ledger independently corroborate the distance is rejected in part: trip_record.actual_distance_km (29.1 km) and fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km (29.1 km) are rounded copies of the same trace measurement, not independent of it. Nothing turns on it, because the optimal distance (22.1 km) is independently set by the routing engine and every artifact carrying a deciding fact is at weight 1.0. The driver's submission calling the deviation 'material' is corrected above; its conclusion is right either way - deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1/329 (0.003) is below 0.05 - so POL-RD-06 gives no full-refund uplift and no conduct referral. No driver compensation is due: the billed 29.1 km falls short of the trace's 29.13 km by 0.03 km, far below the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04. No billing-integrity correction is due under POL-RD-09(4): the gantry is matched to the trace and there is no airport surcharge.\n\nConfidence and next steps. The deciding facts are carried by artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0 (EV-GPS-02804, EV-TRIP-02804, EV-FARE-02804), so confidence is not capped below 1.0 and is set at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: identifiers and timestamps agree, the trace is clean, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited missing artifact, the refund is far below the SGD 150 ceiling and below charged_total, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. The monetary effect, SGD 9.10, exceeds the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the ruling issues and the amount is held for release by a human reviewer under POL-GEN-05. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
